## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design tenant-aware rate limiting and observability in CNF gateways, a realistic production concern for multi-tenant platforms used by large companies.

## Key Concepts

- Tenant-scoped policy API (REST)
- Sidecar token bucket limiter with TTL cache
- Real-time policy fetch and rotation
- Central audit/log sink and schema

## Code Example

```javascript
class TokenBucket {
  constructor(capacity, fillRate) {
    this.capacity = capacity;
    this.fillRate = fillRate;
    this.tokens = capacity;
    this.lastRefill = Date.now();
  }
  allow(n = 1) {
    const now = Date.now();
    const elapsed = (now - this.lastRefill) / 1000;
    this.tokens = Math.min(this.capacity, this.tokens + elapsed * this.fillRate);
    this.lastRefill = now;
    if (this.tokens >= n) {
      this.tokens -= n;
      return true;
    }
    return false;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle policy drift during high load?
- What approaches ensure audit integrity and privacy?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to securely manage per-tenant TLS credentials in a CNF gateway, including secret-driven config, hot-reload of TLS material, and per-tenant mTLS verification.

## Key Concepts

- Kubernetes Secrets mounted as TLS material for sidecars
- Hot-reload of TLS credentials without pod restart
- Mutual TLS with per-tenant CA certificates
- Rotation cadence, error handling, and tenant isolation

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo example: load TLS certs from mounted files and reload on change
let tlsContext = tls.createSecureContext({
  ca: fs.readFileSync('/mnt/cnf-tls/ca.pem'),
  cert: fs.readFileSync('/mnt/cnf-tls/cert.pem'),
  key: fs.readFileSync('/mnt/cnf-tls/key.pem')
});

// watch secret mount and refresh TLS context
fs.watch('/mnt/cnf-tls', () => {
  tlsContext = tls.createSecureContext({
    ca: fs.readFileSync('/mnt/cnf-tls/ca.pem'),
    cert: fs.readFileSync('/mnt/cnf-tls/cert.pem'),
    key: fs.readFileSync('/mnt/cnf-tls/key.pem')
  });
});
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate certificate expiry and revocation in this flow?
- What are the trade-offs between in-cluster secret rotation vs external secret management (e.g., Vault) for CNF gateways?
